## Test Anti-Pattern Audit — Severity-Ranked Findings

This test suite is a textbook example of **"coverage without verification"** — every production method is invoked (achieving line coverage) but almost nothing is actually asserted.

---

### 🔴 Critical — Tests That Prove Nothing

| # | Test | Anti-Pattern | Bug It Misses |
|---|------|-------------|---------------|
| 1 | `AddProduct_Works` (L17-21) | **No assertion at all.** Executes `AddProduct` then exits. | `Save` could silently discard data — test still passes. |
| 2 | `UpdatePrice_Works` (L33-35) | **No assertion.** Calls `UpdatePrice` without verifying the price changed. | Price could remain 9.99 after "update" — test still passes. |
| 3 | `RemoveProduct_Works` (L38-42) | **No assertion.** Calls `RemoveProduct` without verifying deletion. | Product could still exist — test still passes. |
| 4 | `GetProductCount_Works` (L63-66) | **No assertion.** Doesn't even add products first — only proves `GetProductCount` doesn't throw on an empty store. | Could return -1, int.MaxValue, etc. |
| 5 | `ApplyBulkDiscount_Works` (L68-74) | **No assertion.** Never checks that prices actually decreased. | Discount math could be `Price * fraction` (wrong formula) — test still passes. |
| 6 | `ImportFromCsv_Works` (L85-88) | **No assertion.** Never confirms products were actually persisted. | Parser could silently skip lines — test still passes. |

---

### 🟠 High — Weak Assertions (Assert-Not-Null Only)

| # | Test | Problem | Fix |
|---|------|---------|-----|
| 7 | `GetProduct_Works` (L29) | `Assert.IsNotNull` only confirms *something* was returned — not that it's the correct product. | Assert on `Sku`, `Name`, and `Price`. |
| 8 | `SearchProducts_Works` (L51) | Asserts list is non-null but not that it contains "Widget" or excludes "Gadget". | Assert `results.Count == 1 && results[0].Sku == "SKU-001"`. |
| 9 | `ExportToCsv_Works` (L81) | Asserts CSV string is non-null but doesn't validate its content or format. | Assert `csv.Contains("SKU-001,Widget,9.99")`. |
| 10 | `GetAllProducts_Works` (L59) | Asserts list is non-null but doesn't verify its count or contents. | Assert `all.Count == 1`. |

---

### 🟡 Medium — Missing Negative / Edge-Case Tests

| # | Missing Scenario | Production Risk |
|---|-----------------|-----------------|
| 11 | `UpdatePrice` with non-existent SKU | `KeyNotFoundException` path is never exercised. |
| 12 | `GetProduct` for missing SKU | Never verifies null-return behavior. |
| 13 | `ImportFromCsv` with malformed input | Crash on bad CSV (index-out-of-range, parse failure) is never tested. |
| 14 | `ApplyBulkDiscount` with fraction ≥ 1 | Prices could go negative — no guard, no test. |

