### Summary

**Root cause:** Every test follows the pattern *arrange → act → (no assert)*. This inflates code coverage to ~95% while providing near-zero defect detection. The suite would pass identically if every production method were replaced with `{ }`.

**Recommendation:** Treat any test without a value-asserting `Assert.*` call as a coverage-only stub that must be rewritten. Adopt mutation testing (e.g., Stryker.NET) — it would flag all of these immediately.
